# Coding Style, Chapter 1: List of style comments

The source section consists entirely of editorial and TeX coding
conventions. Its twenty-five numbered comments cover line lengths;
indentation; paragraph-start commands; formula line breaking;
displayed-equation delimiters; macros; theorem-environment vocabulary;
environment layout; corollary naming; proof placement; special-file
structure; labels; references to earlier results; cross-file references;
forward references; sentence starts; sentence endings and lead-ins; explicit
hypotheses in statements; proof length; marking defining properties; the
scope of definitions and temporary constructions; equation numbering; short
sentences; section commands; and complicated LaTeX constructions. None of
these comments defines a mathematical object or states a proposition,
identity, diagram, exact sequence, example, hypothesis, or mathematically
meaningful warning. Therefore there is no mathematical declaration to add in
this file.
-/
